 ],
 "method_note": "Fama-MacBeth (1973): one OLS per month across stocks, then the time-series mean of each slope is the premium with a Newey-West (3 lags) standard error. Predictors are winsorized and z-scored within each month, so a slope is the return of a one-standard-deviation tilt. Caveat: the universe is today's constituents (membership history starts 2026-10), so early years carry survivorship bias; read the premium as an upper bound.",
